# Mist adoption snippet - TEMPLATE ONLY.
#
# The real file is gitignored: it carries the org device-id, the outbound-ssh
# secret, a password hash and an SSH key. Anyone holding those could claim
# devices into the org. Export the real snippet from the Mist portal
# (Organization > Inventory > Claim) and save it as mist_claim_set.cfg.
#
# Two edits are required for a vrnetlab-built vJunos node, both applied by
# scripts/push_mist.py - see that file and scripts/push_dns_fix.py:
#   1. outbound-ssh must use the mgmt_junos routing instance
#   2. `delete system phone-home` errors - the node is pre-provisioned
set system services ssh protocol-version v2
set system authentication-order password
set system login user mist class super-user
set system login user mist authentication encrypted-password <REDACTED>
set system login user mist authentication ssh-rsa "<REDACTED>"
set system services outbound-ssh client mist device-id <ORG-UUID>
set system services outbound-ssh client mist secret <REDACTED>
set system services outbound-ssh client mist services netconf keep-alive retry 12 timeout 5
set system services outbound-ssh client mist oc-term.ac2.mist.com port 2200 timeout 60 retry 1000
delete system phone-home
